From: ButterflyOS development <noreply@butterflyos.local>
Subject: [PATCH] refresh battery indicators after watcher notifications

The enhanced power-saving render loop waits for an SDL event while idle.
Battery watcher notifications update cached data but do not wake that loop,
so plugging in or charging can leave the header stale until input or wake.
Request the existing refresh event after publishing changed battery data.
The sleeping-screen path stays asleep; no extra battery polling is added.

Live-tested on the development Flip: unplugging and reconnecting power
updates the charging icon without controller input in about three seconds.

---
--- a/es-core/src/components/ControllerActivityComponent.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/components/ControllerActivityComponent.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "Settings.h"
 #include "utils/Platform.h"
 #include "IExternalActivity.h"
+#include "PowerSaver.h"
 
 #include "watchers/BatteryLevelWatcher.h"
 #include "watchers/NetworkStateWatcher.h"
@@ -35,6 +36,7 @@
 	{
 		mWatchedBatteryInfo = batteryWatcher->getBatteryInfo();
 		mBatteryInfoChanged = true;
+		PowerSaver::pushRefreshEvent();
 	}
 
 	NetworkStateWatcher* networkWatcher = dynamic_cast<NetworkStateWatcher*>(component);
